        "en": "Helpful vets and front desk"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Most clients describe the veterinary surgeons and receptionists as welcoming, friendly, and attentive to their needs. Reviewers appreciate that practitioners listen carefully and manage urgent cases promptly. However, a couple of pet parents report curt or dismissive communication at the front desk when querying test results or administrative matters."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 5,
      "title": {
        "en": "Calm handling for varied animals"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet parents appreciate the gentle handling shown to dogs, cats, and small animals during consultations and routine injections. Reviewers note that nervous dogs remain calm entering the clinic due to the relaxed environment. Several clients also highlight that the clinical team accommodates exotic pets such as ferrets with confidence."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "prices",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 4,
      "title": {
        "en": "Mixed views on clinic fees"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Reviewers share mixed perspectives regarding treatment and consultation costs at the practice. Several pet owners praise the clinic for fair, non-corporate pricing and affordable care compared to other practices in Swords. Conversely, dissatisfied clients express frustration over testing fees, citing costly diagnostic samples and unexpected charges for repeat visits."
      }
    }
